.TH TIMERC-CONFIG 1 "2026" "timerc 1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
timerc-config \- settings, tests and help for timerc, in the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B timerc config
.br
.B timerc config list
.br
.B timerc config get
.I KEY
.br
.B timerc config set
.I KEY VALUE
.br
.B timerc config reset
[\fIKEY\fR]
.br
.B timerc config path
.br
.B timerc about
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without a subcommand,
.B timerc config
opens a full-screen terminal UI with four screens, switched with the number keys:
.TP
.B 1 Settings
Every option, grouped in categories (Alarm, Sleep, Window, Timing, Startup).
Changes are saved immediately and apply to the next timer you start.
.TP
.B 2 Insights
The statistics browser; see
.BR timerc-insights (1).
.TP
.B 3 Test
Audition things without starting a real timer: the alarm, each sleep-mode phase,
the sleep-mode plan for a duration you type, and the fullscreen alert. Output of
the test is shown live; any key stops it.
.TP
.B 4 About
Timer syntax, keys and credits.
.PP
The UI needs only a terminal: no curses library. It redraws on resize, works
down to 32x8 characters, and always restores the terminal on exit (including on
Ctrl+C or a closed connection). When standard input or output is not a terminal,
\fBconfig\fR prints \fBconfig list\fR and \fBabout\fR prints plain text.
.SH KEYS (SETTINGS)
.TP
.BR Up / Down ", " j / k
Select an option.
.TP
.BR Left / Right ", " h / l ", " - / +
Adjust by one step; PgUp/PgDn adjust by ten steps. Toggles flip on/off.
.TP
.B Tab, Shift+Tab
Next / previous category.
.TP
.B Enter
Type an exact value (numbers, or durations such as 1m30s for options measured in
seconds), or toggle a switch.
.TP
.B r, R
Reset the option / reset everything to defaults.
.TP
.B q, Esc, Ctrl+C
Quit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print every option with its value and default.
.TP
.BI get " KEY"
Print one value.
.TP
.BI set " KEY VALUE"
Validate, clamp to the allowed range and save.
.TP
.B reset \fR[\fIKEY\fR]
Restore one option, or all of them, to defaults.
.TP
.B path
Print the path of the configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 for an unknown option or invalid value, 2 for a usage error.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/timerc/config.conf
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
timerc config set alarm_volume_max_percent 60
timerc config get alarm_ramp_seconds
timerc config list | grep sleep
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timerc (1),
.BR timerc-insights (1)
